One (highly risky) option would be to go to the upstairs and wait for
the demon to follow. Repeat this process until you reach a branch of
the dungeon that you don't plan to visit again (mines, soko, or
preferably something a little deeper). Lure the & into this branch and
then dump him there. Of course the demon will be beating on you the
whole way, so you'd better have a lot of HP, a means to restore it
quickly when it gets reduced, a low AC, and counters for all the
special attacks he's likely to throw at you (not to mention the hordes
of other monsters you'll meet along the way.)



